    <briefdescription>
<para>C++ header file with declarations for the µTest++ runner options. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>This header provides the <computeroutput>runner_options</computeroutput> class, which holds the configuration of a test session (the reporter, the verbosity, the output file, the use of colours, the filter, and the listing of the test cases) and parses it from the command line, together with the <computeroutput>reporter_kind</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>verbosity</computeroutput>, and <computeroutput>colour_mode</computeroutput> enumerations used by its members.</para>
<para>The options are usually parsed from the command line by the constructor taking the <computeroutput>main()</computeroutput> arguments, called by <computeroutput>runner::initialise (argc, argv)</computeroutput>; the applications without a command line, such as the embedded ones without semihosting arguments, can set them directly and pass them to <computeroutput>runner::initialise (options)</computeroutput>.</para>
<para>All definitions reside within the <computeroutput><ref refid="namespacemicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus" kindref="compound">micro_os_plus::micro_test_plus</ref></computeroutput> namespace.</para>
<para>The header is included through <computeroutput><ref refid="micro-test-plus_8h" kindref="compound">micro-test-plus.h</ref></computeroutput> and should not be included directly by user code. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
